{"name":"Slime Girl","hex":"#00bb88","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"slime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Soft, moist earth or clay, having an adhesive quality; viscous mud; any substance of a dirty nature, that is moist, soft, and adhesive; bitumen; mud containing metallic ore, obtained in the preparatory dressing.","Any mucilaginous substance; or a mucus-like substance which exudes from the bodies of certain animals, such as snails or slugs."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To coat with slime.","To besmirch or disparage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slime"},{"term":"girl","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female child.","A woman, especially a young and often attractive woman."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To feminize or girlify; to gender as a girl or as for girls.","To staff with or as a girl or girls."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/girl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Slime (monster)","blocks":[{"text":"In fiction, slimes, also called oozes, are amorphous creatures composed of gelatinous ooze. In literature and film, slimes typically take the role of horrific monsters, while in video games and anime, they are often depicted as cute low-level enemies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/OpenGameArt_Slime_Madjestiko.png/330px-OpenGameArt_Slime_Madjestiko.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slime_(monster)"},{"title":"Girl","blocks":[{"text":"A girl is a young female human, usually a child or an adolescent. While the term girl has other meanings, including young woman, daughter, or girlfriend regardless of age, the first meaning is the most common one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg/330px-Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=t